nt proves its identity at the token endpoint (RFC 8705 §2, OIDC Core §9 naming)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Only the methods AXIAM actually implements are representable. "},{"code":"None","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — the public-client"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value — was deliberately absent until T21.2: adding it before the rest of the server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"understood one would have let an operator register a client whose authentication is silently"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"skipped. The server understands one now ("},{"code":"token.rs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"authenticate_client_credential","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an arm that accepts "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" credential and refuses a presented one, the authorization endpoint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"derives its PKCE requirement from this enum, and the admin API refuses the method alongside"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any grant or binding that contradicts it), so the variant exists — and only that arm may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ever treat a missing credential as success."}]}}}